1
00:00:00,660 --> 00:00:05,260
Runbooks drift from the code, and
nobody notices until an incident.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:09,740
In the Q1 2025 SlashData
developer survey, 31% of

3
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:15,075
developers named insufficient or
outdated documentation a top challenge.

4
00:00:15,115 --> 00:00:17,635
In organisations with
over a thousand employees

5
00:00:17,675 --> 00:00:21,715
involved in software projects, it was 46%.

6
00:00:21,755 --> 00:00:25,395
And Atlassian's State of
Teams 2024 found that 55%

7
00:00:25,435 --> 00:00:28,195
of knowledge workers find it
hard to track down information.

8
00:00:28,235 --> 00:00:32,323
A runbook you cannot
trust makes that worse.

9
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:37,590
This is The Page Is Lying,
a Forge app for Confluence.

10
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:40,900
An admin points it at a
public GitHub repository,

11
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:44,310
here the payments API,
and it indexes the code.

12
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:48,431
The check is read-only, it
runs on the Forge free tier,

13
00:00:48,471 --> 00:00:51,041
and there is no language
model in the check.

14
00:00:51,111 --> 00:00:53,921
It is regular expressions
and a code index.

15
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,820
Here is a real runbook.

16
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:59,060
The macro reads the claims
in this section and

17
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,860
compares each one with the
code at a pinned commit.

18
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,860
Two claims are verified in code,

19
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:07,845
three are contradicted by code,
and one has no evidence found.

20
00:01:07,885 --> 00:01:11,765
The first paragraph tells
readers to call POST /v1/charge.

21
00:01:11,805 --> 00:01:16,885
It is contradicted by code: no route
matches, and the repository has

22
00:01:16,925 --> 00:01:21,765
POST /v2/payments at
src/routes.ts, line 88.

23
00:01:21,805 --> 00:01:25,910
The environment variable
STRIPE_KEY is contradicted too.

24
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:32,710
The code reads PAYMENTS_API_KEY
at src/config.ts, line 8.

25
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:35,670
The refund command with the
force flag is contradicted:

26
00:01:35,710 --> 00:01:38,645
refund defines confirm and reason instead.

27
00:01:38,685 --> 00:01:42,565
Two claims are verified in code,
with the file and line cited.

28
00:01:42,605 --> 00:01:46,405
The last one, ledgerctl
reconcile, is grey.

29
00:01:46,445 --> 00:01:47,765
No evidence found.

30
00:01:47,805 --> 00:01:49,205
That is not a confirmation.

31
00:01:49,245 --> 00:01:53,861
Every state has an icon and
a label, not just a colour.

32
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:58,580
Hover or tab to a claim and
a card shows the evidence,

33
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:01,860
with a permalink to the
exact line on GitHub.

34
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:03,350
Escape closes it.

35
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:08,100
The same check is available in Rovo.

36
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:12,980
The Runbook checker agent can only report
what its read-only action returned.

37
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:17,350
I ask, can I still call POST /v1/charge?

38
00:02:17,695 --> 00:02:21,095
The answer: no, contradicted by code.

39
00:02:21,135 --> 00:02:23,015
No route matches.

40
00:02:23,055 --> 00:02:29,981
The repository has POST /v2/payments
at src/routes.ts, line 88,

41
00:02:30,021 --> 00:02:36,351
with an evidence id, the repository, the
commit, the counts and the coverage limits.

42
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:42,660
The app also exposes five read-only
tools through a Forge MCP server.

43
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:46,260
Here is an MCP client,
signed in over OAuth.

44
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:50,593
It lists check-page and check-claim,
and returns the same verdicts,

45
00:02:50,633 --> 00:02:54,353
the same file and line,
and the same evidence ids.

46
00:02:54,393 --> 00:02:58,003
Same tool, same evidence, any MCP client.

47
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:01,340
Now we fix the page.

48
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:06,620
Change the first claim to POST
/v2/payments, publish, and reload.

49
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:14,380
That paragraph is verified in code,
citing src/routes.ts, line 88.

50
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:17,309
The counts are now three verified,

51
00:03:17,349 --> 00:03:21,279
two contradicted by code, and
one with no evidence found.

52
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:25,870
For a contradicted claim
you can draft a Jira task.

53
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:28,780
The app shows the exact issue text first.

54
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:33,740
It writes nothing itself: Open
Jira create screen only opens

55
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:37,390
Jira with that text filled in,
and you create the issue there.

56
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:43,100
Deterministic, cites file
and line, read-only,

57
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:46,380
and it works on any
public GitHub repository.

58
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:48,270
The Page Is Lying.

59
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:50,980
Documentation that checks
itself against the code.
